   2 0 0  0  0 \t | # start a recipe context, as in GNU Make: the tab-indented ## line after them is a recipe
   3 0 0  0  0 \t | # line, so next-N keeps its inline doc. Known bug #181: after an assignment, the ## line
   4 0 0  0  0 \t | # is read as a doc, which replaces the inline doc of next-N.
